  "tagline": "Forty-six villas with private pools on a lagoon island, reached by seaplane.",
  "description": "Cheval Blanc Randheli is a Maldivian island hotel of 46 villas, each with an infinity-edge pool, designed by the architect Jean-Michel Gathy. Guests arrive by seaplane or speedboat from Malé, and the hotel runs its own seaplane in the brand's taupe and yellow.\n\nThe hotel spreads across six islands in a turquoise lagoon, with ivory beaches and a spa on an island of its own. Gathy designed the villas as private residences open to the outdoors, with furnishings of rattan, bamboo and mother of pearl in pop yellow, taupe and white. Vincent Beaurin's Arch, a monumental copper form, rises from the lagoon, and each villa carries a work called Couronne.\n\nThe villas include the 1-Bedroom Water Villa, 220 square metres on stilts over the water, with an overwater deck and a 12.5-metre private infinity pool. The 1-Bedroom Island Villa covers 240 square metres on the beach, with a garden, a dining pergola and a pool of the same length. Other types are Lagoon, Horizon and Garden Water Villas, and the two-bedroom Island, Garden Water and Lagoon Garden Villas, for four guests. Each villa has a dedicated majordome.\n\nFive restaurants and three bars serve the island. Deelani stands over the water and serves Italian cooking. Diptyque serves Japanese and East Asian dishes at dinner from Friday to Sunday, and Le 1947 offers an 11-course French tasting menu from Monday to Wednesday. A wine museum and cigar lounge, and in-villa dining at any hour, complete the choice.\n\nThe Cheval Blanc Spa offers Guerlain treatments and is open from 10 am to 9 pm, with a hair spa by Leonor Greyl on the spa island. The White has an infinity pool and a bar, yoga is taught on the sand and in an overwater pavilion, and there is a surf simulator, the only one in the Maldives. Guests can drift through the coral gardens, take a Dhoni cruise at sunset or watch a film under the stars, and Le Carrousel looks after children.\n\nThe island suits couples and families who want a private villa with its own pool and a beach in front of it.",
